    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "BT10-058",
        "question": "What happens to the cards that weren't added to my hand from among the cards revealed by this card’s effects?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can.  In such cases, you add as many cards to your hand as possible.",
        "question": "This card’s effect reveals 4 cards. If the cards revealed only include 1 card that is either black with [Knightmon] or 1 card with the [Twilight] trait, can I still add a card to my hand?",
        "reference": "[2]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No. This card's effect reads “Add 2 cards [...] among them to your hand,” so you must add as many cards to your hand as possible. However, if you have a black card with [Knightmon] and the [Twilight] trait among the revealed cards and there are no other cards with [Knightmon], you can treat that card as your card with the [Twilight] trait and add it to your hand. Any other cards that have the [Twilight] trait will then be returned to the bottom of your deck. In such a case, it can be possible to add just 1 of the cards.",
        "question": "This card's effect reveals 4 cards. If 2 cards that are either black with [Knightmon] and/or the [Twilight] trait are among the cards revealed, can I choose to only add one of them to my hand, and place the remaining card at the bottom of my deck?",
        "reference": "[2]"
      }
    ]
  },
